module gunbc.measurement_provenance

import std.types { Bool, String }

import gunbc.devboot.outcome {
  BuildExecutionOutcome,
  ArtifactAvailability,
  ArtifactAvailable,
  ArtifactMissing,
  ArtifactCorrupt,
  ArtifactUnreadable,
  StoredArtifact,
  StoredArtifactRecord,
  DevbootWorkStatus,
}

data measurement_provenance_root_note: String = "FOUR SPECIMENS, ONE ABSENT RELATION, ONE DAY (2026-08-20, this fleet). (1) A stale binary produced first_generation_equal=true — tree and compiler were different vintages and nothing in the receipt said so. (2) A DIFFERENT stale binary produced a 9-declaration drop that did not exist, escalated through three sessions before execution refuted it byte-identical across 131 files — the binary had been replaced mid-sequence as collateral from an unrelated all-bins build, and the author never typed a command that built it. (3) `cargo build 2>&1 | tail -4 && next` takes tail's exit status, so a FAILED build proceeded as success and the downstream step measured a stale artifact. (4) A treatment merge hit 'refusing to merge unrelated histories' on a shallow clone; unguarded, the baseline numbers would have re-reported as the treatment arm. Every one returned a plausible, well-formed number. Every one was caught by a person noticing an inconsistency, never by a mechanism. The root is not 'stale binaries' — it is one relation, absent in all four: a reported observation is not structurally bound to the SUCCESSFUL CONSTRUCTION of its exact instrument and its exact subject. This module makes the unbound observation unrepresentable rather than checkable."

data measurement_provenance_construction_not_validation_note: String = "THE SHAPE THIS MODULE REFUSES TO BE: a function whose job is to verify that a measurement carries its provenance. If such a function can exist, the bad state was already writable and this would be a validator standing where construction belongs (DESIGN section 5). Instead Observation<Value> is a coproduct whose bound arm (Observed) is reachable ONLY by folding two retrievability observations that both landed on ArtifactAvailable. The unbound arms carry no StoredArtifact: there is nothing to copy forward, so a caller cannot manufacture instrument or subject identity for a build that did not produce retrievable bytes. observe is the ONLY constructor of Observed; no other function in this module builds one."

data measurement_provenance_authority_note: String = "WHY THIS MODULE MINTS NO OUTCOME VOCABULARY OF ITS OWN. An earlier revision of this carrier declared its own InstrumentConstruction and SubjectConstruction coproducts, each collapsing every way a construction can fail into one NonEmptyStr detail. That was a second and strictly poorer authority for a concept gunbc.devboot.outcome already owns (DESIGN section 3), and the poverty was not cosmetic: devboot keeps BuildFailureCause and InfrastructureRefusalCause deliberately APART because a compilation failure is a fact about the subject and retrying changes nothing, while an infrastructure refusal is a fact about this host at this moment and the same subject may succeed later — fusing them makes 'is retry pointless' unanswerable, which is precisely what a single detail string does. Specimen (4), a subject that could not be fetched, exists there as the TYPE InfrastructureRefusalCause SubjectNotFetchable rather than as a sentence. So this module imports that authority and contributes only what devboot does not model: the binding of a reported Value to the identities of the instrument that produced it and the subject it was taken of. devboot answers 'may a caller believe it holds these bytes'; this module answers 'may a caller believe this number was produced by that instrument from that subject', and it answers it by having no arm in which the number travels without both."

data measurement_provenance_stale_instrument_note: String = "WHAT THE FOLD ONTO devboot CLOSED, WHICH THIS CARRIER PREVIOUSLY DECLARED OUT OF REACH. Specimen (1) is a PAST successful build being read as evidence about a PRESENT binary. The earlier revision named that axis outside the modeled guarantee and stopped there. devboot had already split it on purpose: execution is history and availability is an observation of the store, ArtifactAvailable carries the read-back that established it, and availability_permits_retrieval reads the availability axis ALONE so that a past success contributes nothing to whether bytes can be had now. observe therefore selects its arm on availability alone and never on execution — an ExecutionProduced whose artifact is Missing, Corrupt or Unreadable yields a refusal, not an Observed — which is specimen (1)'s shape refused by construction rather than declared unmodeled. Execution is still CARRIED into the refusal arms, because that is where the retry question is answered; it simply has no vote on whether the observation binds."

data measurement_provenance_source_vintage_note: String = "FOUR MORE SPECIMENS, SIX DAYS LATER, ONE MODE THIS CARRIER DID NOT CLOSE (2026-08-26, this fleet). In one night four sessions independently produced false BLOCKING defect reports about a healthy main. Three were the modes already modeled here — a baked binary of an older vintage, and a check that returned CLEAN because the entry compiled did not reach the stage that produces the diagnostic. The fourth was not: a binary that was FRESHLY BUILT, retrievable, uncorrupted and passing every freshness probe on offer, from a WORKTREE fourteen commits behind main. Its bytes were beyond reproach; the source they were built from was stale, and it refused three channels that current main models. The earlier revision of this carrier could not have said so. Its Observed arm carried StoredArtifact, whose only subject-identity field is subject_digest — which devboot's own header calls an index rather than a proof — so a measurement was bound to bytes and to nothing about the tree those bytes came from. Carrying StoredArtifactRecord instead binds tree_oid into the bound arm, so two instruments built from different trees are now distinguishable AT the observation rather than by a reader remembering to check. WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT CLAIM: it makes the vintage REPRESENTABLE and CARRIED where it was previously absent, which is what lets a consumer compare it; it does not by itself refuse a stale instrument, because which tree a measurement ought to have been taken from is a fact about the reader's question and not about the store. That comparison is the consumer's, and this carrier's job is to make it possible to state."

data measurement_provenance_status_pairing_note: String = "A SECOND HAZARD CLOSED BY THE SAME SIGNATURE CHANGE, AND IT IS NOT THE ONE THE WORK STARTED FROM. The earlier observe took four loose axes — instrument execution, instrument availability, subject execution, subject availability — so a caller could pair one build's execution with another build's availability and no arm could refuse: the fold selects on availability, and the refusal it returns then reports the OTHER build's answer to 'is retry pointless'. Every arm would have been well-formed and the mis-pairing invisible. DevbootWorkStatus is devboot's own binding of the two axes to the request they describe, so taking two statuses makes the mismatch unwritable rather than undetected. Recorded separately from the vintage note because it was found by writing the signature rather than by the specimens, and a hazard folded silently into another finding's story is one nobody can later check."

data measurement_provenance_boundary_note: String = "THE HONEST BOUNDARY THAT REMAINS, NARROWED BUT NOT CLOSED. What is structural: no Observation can carry a Value alongside an instrument or subject identity unless both retrievability observations landed on ArtifactAvailable, and the identities it carries are StoredArtifact values taken out of those arms rather than assembled here. What is NOT structural: whether the ArtifactAvailable handed to observe was itself established by a read-back performed by THIS invocation against the path actually used, rather than hand-authored with a fabricated Sha256Digest by a caller who bypassed the store entirely. devboot states that contract for its own producers; nothing in the type system enforces it against an arbitrary caller, and that is the same residual gap sole_constructor already names as unverified for generic carriers. So the wet boundary has moved — from 'no read-back is modeled at all' to 'the read-back is modeled and required, and its authenticity rests on an unverified construction ceiling' — and DESIGN section 4b's rule is to say which rung that is rather than claim a uniform climb. A SECOND RESIDUE, NAMED BECAUSE THIS REVISION MOVED IT RATHER THAN CLOSED IT: the StoredArtifactRecord the bound arm carries is assembled here from ONE DevbootWorkStatus — its subject paired with the artifact its own availability arm observed — rather than taken out of the store as a record. That pairing is faithful to what a status means, since both fields answer for the same work id; it is not the store's own read-back of the record, so a caller who hand-authored a status can still hand-author the pairing. The vintage is now carried and comparable, which is strictly more than it was; its authenticity rests on the same unverified construction ceiling as the digest above, and not on a stronger one. The practical discipline this does not replace: freeze the instrument outside the build tree before first measurement and invoke it by absolute path, because a binary can be silently replaced by an unrelated command between the observation and the measurement."

data measurement_provenance_adoption_note: String = "ADOPTION STATUS, STATED RATHER THAN IMPLIED. Nothing in the accepted program folds through observe today, and the fold onto devboot did not change that: measured on this branch, gunbc.devboot is itself imported by four of its own siblings and three witness tests, and by no production consumer anywhere. So this carrier and the authority it now shares are one unconsumed cluster rather than two, which is progress in modeling and none in consumption. That is worth stating plainly because the precedent this design was originally argued from does NOT have that property — gunbc.regen_receipt earns its keep because required_regen_host folds the actual regen path through it — and a citation whose force depends on a consumption fact the citation does not carry is itself a specimen of this module's subject. The trigger for adoption is the first measurement site that needs a number bound to its instrument and subject; binding one is a separate packet scoped against a real wet path, not an addition to this carrier, and a caller invented here to occupy the consumer slot would be a fabricated consumer — the exact class this module exists to refuse."

// THE REPORTED FACT, BOUND OR REFUSED. Observation<Value> is generic over the reported
// number/fact so this carrier is not re-minted per measurement site (DESIGN section 2 — one
// concept, every breadth). Observed is the only arm carrying a Value, and it is the only arm
// carrying identities; the two unbound arms carry the two devboot axes instead, so a refusal
// says both what could not be had NOW (availability) and whether retrying is pointless
// (execution). A plausible Value with no bound instrument or subject has no constructor here.
//
// THE BOUND ARM CARRIES StoredArtifactRecord RATHER THAN StoredArtifact, and that is the whole
// content of this revision. StoredArtifact's only subject-identity field is subject_digest,
// which gunbc.devboot.outcome declares in its own words to be an INDEX so a candidate can be
// found and explicitly NOT what decides whether the candidate is the right one. An Observed
// built on it therefore bound a Value to some bytes and to nothing about where those bytes came
// from. StoredArtifactRecord is devboot's existing pairing of those bytes with the full
// BuildSubject they were built for — including tree_oid, the source vintage — so the identity
// the observation carries is now the one devboot itself uses to decide identity, and no second
// vocabulary is minted to say so (DESIGN section 3).
type Observation<Value>
  = Observed { instrument: StoredArtifactRecord, subject: StoredArtifactRecord, value: Value }
  | InstrumentNotHeld { execution: BuildExecutionOutcome, availability: ArtifactAvailability }
  | SubjectNotHeld { execution: BuildExecutionOutcome, availability: ArtifactAvailability }

// THE SOLE CONSTRUCTOR OF Observed. It selects on availability ALONE, agreeing with devboot's
// availability_permits_retrieval by construction rather than by restating its rule — the arms
// here exist to extract the StoredArtifact that the Bool-returning authority cannot hand back,
// and the witness asserts the two agree on every arm so the agreement is executed, not assumed.
//
// IT TAKES TWO DevbootWorkStatus VALUES RATHER THAN FOUR LOOSE AXES, which closes a second
// hazard the earlier signature left open and which no arm could have refused. With execution
// and availability arriving as independent parameters, nothing stopped a caller pairing build
// A's execution with build B's availability: the fold would have selected on B and reported
// A's retry answer, and every arm would have looked well-formed. A status is devboot's own
// pairing of the two axes with the request they belong to, so the mismatch is now unwritable
// rather than undetected (DESIGN section 5 — construction over validation).
//
// The instrument is decided before the subject, so an instrument refusal is reported over a
// subject one when both are unavailable — an arbitrary but declared tie-break, not a silent
// drop of the second failure. A caller wanting both still holds both statuses; this fold
// reports one typed refusal rather than a merged one (DESIGN section 5: a failure arm must
// refuse, never widen).
fn observe<Value>(
  instrument: DevbootWorkStatus,
  subject: DevbootWorkStatus,
  value: Value,
) -> Observation<Value> {
  match instrument.availability {
    ArtifactMissing =>
      InstrumentNotHeld { execution: instrument.execution, availability: instrument.availability }
    ArtifactCorrupt { expected, observed } =>
      InstrumentNotHeld { execution: instrument.execution, availability: instrument.availability }
    ArtifactUnreadable { detail } =>
      InstrumentNotHeld { execution: instrument.execution, availability: instrument.availability }
    ArtifactAvailable { artifact: instrument_artifact } =>
      match subject.availability {
        ArtifactMissing =>
          SubjectNotHeld { execution: subject.execution, availability: subject.availability }
        ArtifactCorrupt { expected, observed } =>
          SubjectNotHeld { execution: subject.execution, availability: subject.availability }
        ArtifactUnreadable { detail } =>
          SubjectNotHeld { execution: subject.execution, availability: subject.availability }
        ArtifactAvailable { artifact: subject_artifact } =>
          Observed {
            instrument: StoredArtifactRecord {
              subject: instrument.subject,
              artifact: instrument_artifact,
            },
            subject: StoredArtifactRecord {
              subject: subject.subject,
              artifact: subject_artifact,
            },
            value: value,
          }
      }
  }
}

fn observation_is_bound<Value>(o: Observation<Value>) -> Bool {
  match o {
    Observed { instrument, subject, value } => true
    InstrumentNotHeld { execution, availability } => false
    SubjectNotHeld { execution, availability } => false
  }
}
